{"crc":"07bc3894","kind":"Candidate","payload":{"response":"Looking at the issue, the problem is in `check_for_template_tags_with_the_same_name` function. When a template tag library is specified in `TEMPLATES['OPTIONS']['libraries']`, it gets added to the `libraries` defaultdict. Then `get_template_tag_modules()` also returns the same module (since it scans installed apps), causing a duplicate entry for the same module path.\n\nThe fix should deduplicate the module paths for each library name before checking if there are multiple entries. Here's the fix:\n\n# path: django/core/checks/templates.py\n```\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n    for library_name, items in libraries.items():\n        if len(items) > 1:\n            errors.append(\n                Error(\n                    E003.msg.format(\n                        repr(library_name),\n                        \", \".join(repr(item) for item in items),\n                    ),\n                    id=E003.id,\n                )\n            )\n=======\n    for library_name, items in libraries.items():\n        unique_items = list(dict.fromkeys(items))\n        if len(unique_items) > 1:\n            errors.append(\n                Error(\n                    E003.msg.format(\n                        repr(library_name),\n                        \", \".join(repr(item) for item in unique_items),\n                    ),\n                    id=E003.id,\n                )\n            )\n>>>>>>> REPLACE\n```","round":1,"slot":0},"producer":{"instance":"01KZQX9QGY7FASTATNRQ2T9PP3","kind":"drafter","parent":"01KZQX9QGS7EV7M1V7A85FYQN7"},"schema":"Candidate@1","seq":14,"t":1786435145.95805}
{"crc":"2b56a468","kind":"substrate.TriggerFired","payload":{"factory":"validator","firing_key":null,"input_sha256":"sha256:a78e20d7b58ad4ef8bcb07a084218cc4022705a596a22c7e0ff65f45a9b83544","instance":"01KZQXA476ZWT30PN70MBHFAHV","resolved_input":{"response":"Looking at the issue, the problem is in `check_for_template_tags_with_the_same_name` function. When a template tag library is specified in `TEMPLATES['OPTIONS']['libraries']`, it gets added to the `libraries` defaultdict. Then `get_template_tag_modules()` also returns the same module (since it scans installed apps), causing a duplicate entry for the same module path.\n\nThe fix should deduplicate the module paths for each library name before checking if there are multiple entries. Here's the fix:\n\n# path: django/core/checks/templates.py\n```\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n    for library_name, items in libraries.items():\n        if len(items) > 1:\n            errors.append(\n                Error(\n                    E003.msg.format(\n                        repr(library_name),\n                        \", \".join(repr(item) for item in items),\n                    ),\n                    id=E003.id,\n                )\n            )\n=======\n    for library_name, items in libraries.items():\n        unique_items = list(dict.fromkeys(items))\n        if len(unique_items) > 1:\n            errors.append(\n                Error(\n                    E003.msg.format(\n                        repr(library_name),\n                        \", \".join(repr(item) for item in unique_items),\n                    ),\n                    id=E003.id,\n                )\n            )\n>>>>>>> REPLACE\n```","round":1,"slot":0},"trigger_id":"validate"},"producer":null,"schema":"substrate.TriggerFired@1","seq":15,"t":1786435145.9581802}
